Subject: [PATCH] platform: define SDL_PLATFORM_SUBSTRATE

Substrate is an ELF Unix with its own ELFOSABI (0x40) and its own cross
toolchain, which predefines __substrate__ and __unix__ but NOT __linux__.
SDL already sets SDL_PLATFORM_UNIX from __unix__, so the build is not
adrift -- but there is no macro naming the platform itself, and the audio
code below needs one to pick substrate's device path.

Declare SDL_PLATFORM_SUBSTRATE the same way every other platform is
declared.  No behaviour changes on any other target.

--- a/include/SDL3/SDL_platform_defines.h
+++ b/include/SDL3/SDL_platform_defines.h
@@ -126,6 +126,19 @@
 #define SDL_PLATFORM_UNIX 1
 #endif
 
+#ifdef __substrate__
+
+/**
+ * A preprocessor macro that is only defined if compiling for Substrate.
+ *
+ * Substrate is an ELF Unix with its own OSABI; its cross compiler predefines
+ * `__substrate__` and `__unix__`, so SDL_PLATFORM_UNIX is set as well.
+ *
+ * \since This macro is available since SDL 3.2.0.
+ */
+#define SDL_PLATFORM_SUBSTRATE 1
+#endif
+
 #ifdef __APPLE__
 
 /**
